1
00:03:26,470 --> 00:03:32,470
In space no one can hear you scream.

2
00:06:52,941 --> 00:06:58,941
Alien is a horror, science fiction film directed by Ridley Scott.

3
00:10:19,411 --> 00:10:25,411
During its return to the earth, commercial spaceship Nostromo
intercepts a distress signal from a distant planet.

4
00:13:45,882 --> 00:13:51,882
When a three-member team of the crew discovers a chamber containing thousands of eggs
on the planet, a creature inside one of the eggs attacks an explorer.

5
00:17:12,352 --> 00:17:18,352
The entire crew is unaware of the impending nightmare set to descend upon them when
the alien parasite planted inside its unfortunate host is birthed.

6
00:20:38,823 --> 00:20:44,823
Dallas, played by Tom Skerritt.

7
00:24:05,294 --> 00:24:11,294
Ripley, played by Sigourney Weaver.

8
00:27:31,764 --> 00:27:37,764
Lambert, played by Veronica Cartwright.

9
00:30:58,235 --> 00:31:04,235
Brett, played by Harry Dean Stanton.

10
00:34:24,705 --> 00:34:30,705
Kane, played by John Hurt.

11
00:37:51,176 --> 00:37:57,176
Ash, played by Ian Holm.

12
00:41:17,647 --> 00:41:23,647
Alien is a 1979 science fiction horror film directed by Ridley Scott and written
by Dan O'Bannon, based on a story by O'Bannon and Ronald Shusett.

13
00:44:44,117 --> 00:44:50,117
It follows a commercial starship crew who investigate a derelict space
vessel and are hunted by a deadly extraterrestrial creature.

14
00:48:10,588 --> 00:48:16,588
The film stars Tom Skerritt, Sigourney Weaver, Veronica Cartwright,
Harry Dean Stanton, John Hurt, Ian Holm, and Yaphet Kotto.

15
00:51:37,058 --> 00:51:43,058
It was produced by Gordon Carroll, David Giler, and Walter Hill through their
company Brandywine Productions and was distributed by 20th Century-Fox.

16
00:55:03,529 --> 00:55:09,529
Giler and Hill revised and made additions to the
script; Shusett was the executive producer.

17
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
The alien creatures and environments were designed by the Swiss artist H.

18
01:01:56,470 --> 01:02:02,470
Giger, while the concept artists Ron Cobb and
Chris Foss designed the other sets.

19
01:05:22,941 --> 01:05:28,941
Alien premiered on May 25, 1979, the opening night of the
fourth Seattle International Film Festival.

20
01:08:49,411 --> 01:08:55,411
It received a wide release on June 22 and was released
on September 6 in the United Kingdom.

21
01:12:15,882 --> 01:12:21,882
It initially received mixed reviews, but won the Academy Award for Best Visual Effects, three Saturn Awards (Best Science Fiction Film,
Best Direction for Scott, and Best Supporting Actress for Cartwright), and a Hugo Award for Best Dramatic Presentation.

22
01:15:42,352 --> 01:15:48,352
Alien grossed $78.9 million in the United States and £7.8 million in
the United Kingdom during its first theatrical run.

23
01:19:08,823 --> 01:19:14,823
Its worldwide gross has been estimated at between $104 million and $188 million.

24
01:22:35,294 --> 01:22:41,294
In subsequent years, Alien was critically reassessed and is now considered one of the
greatest and most influential science fiction and horror films of all time.

25
01:26:01,764 --> 01:26:07,764
In 2002, Alien was deemed "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant" by the Library of
Congress and was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry.

26
01:29:28,235 --> 01:29:34,235
In 2008, it was ranked by the American Film Institute as the seventh-best film in the
science fiction genre, and as the 33rd-greatest film of all time by Empire.

27
01:32:54,705 --> 01:33:00,705
The success of Alien spawned a media franchise of films, books, video
games, and toys, and propelled Weaver's acting career.

28
01:36:21,176 --> 01:36:27,176
The story of her character's encounters with the alien creatures became the thematic and narrative
core of the sequels Aliens (1986), Alien 3 (1992), and Alien Resurrection (1997).

29
01:39:47,647 --> 01:39:53,647
A crossover with the Predator franchise produced the Alien vs.

30
01:43:14,117 --> 01:43:20,117
Predator films, while a two-film prequel series was directed by Scott before
Alien: Romulus (2024), a standalone sequel, was released.

31
01:46:40,588 --> 01:46:46,588
A television prequel written by Noah Hawley and produced by Scott,
Alien: Earth, was released on FX on Hulu on August 12, 2025.

32
01:50:07,058 --> 01:50:13,058
The film explores themes of android, spacecraft,
space marine, biology, dystopia.

33
01:53:33,529 --> 01:53:39,529
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
